  "contract": [
    "Release eleven nullable cells at offsets94,a8,b8,c8,1c,2c,3c,4c,5c,74,84 in that order. Each nonzero cell is cleared only after release. Reload the canonical owner for every field.",
    "Release buffers at6c and70 even when zero, without clearing those slots. Reload the owner again; if nonnull release it then clear the owner and return0, otherwise return0x10000005.",
    "Public thunk aliases the destructor. The HRV frame-status adapter ignores its frame argument and returns0 for success or-1 for nonzero status. The cell helper always returns0 when it returns."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "All168 native instruction bytes execute in49152 field-mask comparisons,120 live-owner/result mutations and18 direct cell-helper comparisons. Callback snapshots establish clear-after-free timing.",
    "1440 comparisons execute the actual C initializer/malloc/free and new HRV teardown. Typed contexts are fixture preparation, not a recovered HRV initializer. Context-before/after-children layouts, optional unrelated guard allocations, and full heap/context writes are checked.",
    "Initial-null parent access at0x94 and null cell-helper access at0 are checked as unmapped reads in the emulator. This is an access-shape check, not a claim about MCU flash mapping or physical fault behavior. The initial context must be valid for supported teardown.",
    "Direct tests model free and caller-scratch clobbers; actual-heap integration has no source stock-code fallback. Saved integer/FP registers, SP, masks, FPSCR and guards are checked. Caller scratch/private frames/APSR excluded.",
    "One canonical four-byte HRV context owner added, with no new imports. Source plan/cache layout and prior portable API utilities unchanged. Future native HRV initialization must share this owner.",
    "No allocator deinit body is inferred solely from SDK declarations. Observed pool-cell xrefs are not proof of exhaustive indirect-reference coverage. Remaining algorithm initialization/computation/teardown, concurrency, physical memory, final linking/startup and boot remain open."
